## Traps

- **A green subagent report is not a green run.** L8 reported "all 21 hooks Passed"; the verifying
  run exited 1 on two hooks. Always re-run the gate yourself.
- **`pre-commit run --all-files` and the commit-time hook can disagree.** Root cause was five
  competing isort configs (fixed in #2028). If it recurs, compare `known_first_party` across
  root + the three per-package `[tool.isort]` blocks.
- **`git status --porcelain` counts staged AND unstaged** — `'^ M\|^.M'` matches both; it will
  mislead you about what a hook just modified.
- **Bash working directory PERSISTS between calls.** A stray `cd packages/...` silently made an
  `isort --show-config` reading come from the wrong package; it produced a confident wrong
  conclusion that had to be retracted. Re-anchor with an absolute `cd` when measuring config.
- **`#2011` fires during pre-commit itself** — the Tier-1 hook reports "files were modified"
  because `packages/kailash-kaizen/scripts/test_examples_implementation.py` writes
  `kaizen_implementation_test.log` into the repo root at import. L6 identified the fix: RENAME the
  file (the `test_` prefix IS the bug — it collects zero tests) + move `logging.basicConfig` into
  `__main__`. Sibling `comprehensive_implementation_tester.py` has the same latent shape.
- **#2029** — `test_concurrent_execution_performance` is a load-sensitive flake in the Tier-1
  pre-commit hook (asserts 3x on a ~30ms workload). It will block commits on a busy machine.
  Do NOT widen the threshold.
- `.env` `OPENAI_API_KEY` is INVALID (live 401). Anthropic works.
- Tests: ALWAYS `.venv/bin/python -m pytest`. An errored run is zero evidence, not a failure.

